  "id": "solow-swan-growth-model-eco",
  "name": "Solow-Swan Growth Model",
  "description": "Foundational neoclassical model of long-term economic growth. Capital accumulation drives growth in output per worker, but diminishing returns to capital mean the economy converges to a steady state. Long-run growth requires technological progress. Reference: Solow, R. M. (1956). A contribution to the theory of economic growth. Quarterly Journal of Economics, 70(1), 65-94. DOI: https://doi.org/10.2307/1884513",
